  "explanation": {
    "short": "rr is a rolled r (a single r is one quick tap); ll is a heavy, dark l; y is an i said with round lips, like German ü. c is ts, x is dz, xh is the j of \"jam\", zh is the s of \"measure\", and j is the y of \"yes\".",
    "more": "The tricky pairs are c and ç (ts versus ch) and x and xh (dz versus j). Albanian j is not English j: jam is \"yam\", not \"jam\". Every letter has one sound, so these are rules you can trust."
  },
